---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const datasetSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "needle-bench AI Coding Agent Benchmark",
  "description": "Open benchmark for AI coding agents. Real bugs as frozen Docker snapshots, deterministic scoring across native CLI, kernel (OpenRouter) and CPU (native driver) arms.",
  "url": "https://needle-bench.cc/",
  "license": "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT",
  "keywords": ["AI coding benchmark", "LLM evaluation", "agent benchmark", "debugging benchmark", "Docker bugs", "Claude", "GPT", "Gemini", "DeepSeek"],
  "creator": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "os-tack",
    "url": "https://github.com/os-tack"
  },
  "distribution": {
    "@type": "DataDownload",
    "encodingFormat": "application/json",
    "contentUrl": "https://needle-bench.cc/experiment-scores.json"
  }
};
---

<Base
  title="needle-bench — AI coding agent leaderboard on real Docker bugs"
  description="Open benchmark for AI coding agents. v7.6.0: 8 frontier models × 38 real-bug Docker benchmarks, native vendor CLI vs ostk kernel. Resolved-gated, per-bucket cost. Deterministic scoring."
  jsonLd={datasetSchema}
>
  <main>
    <h1 class="visually-hidden">needle-bench AI Coding Agent Leaderboard</h1>
    <div class="experiment-info">
      <p><strong>v7.6.0 &mdash; native vendor CLI vs ostk kernel.</strong> 8 frontier models &times; 38 benchmarks, single-shot (samples=1), captured 2026-06-15. Cost/token &Delta; are resolved-gated (cells both arms solved), per-bucket priced, and shown <em>only</em> for Anthropic &mdash; the one native harness that reports cost.</p>
      <p class="muted">Cost &Delta; / Token &Delta; = kernel vs native (<span style="color:#3fb950">negative = kernel cheaper/lighter</span>). Click headers to sort. <a href="/v760.html">Full per-cell detail &amp; methodology &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="lb-container" id="lb-container">
      <table id="lb">
        <thead>
          <tr id="lb-head">
            <th class="col-model" data-key="model">Model</th>
            <th data-key="type" title="B = true kernel (native CpuDriver); B* = generic OpenRouter kernel">Type</th>
            <th data-key="native_cli">Native CLI</th>
            <th class="col-solve arm-native" data-key="native_pct">Native solve</th>
            <th class="col-solve arm-cpu" data-key="kernel_pct">Kernel solve</th>
            <th class="col-metric arm-cpu" data-key="cost_delta" title="kernel vs native cost, both-solved cells (Anthropic only)">Cost &Delta;</th>
            <th class="col-metric arm-cpu" data-key="tok_delta" title="kernel vs native tokens, both-solved cells (Anthropic only)">Token &Delta;</th>
            <th data-key="notes">Notes</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="lb-body">
          <tr><td colspan="8" class="empty">Loading...</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="bstar-note muted"><sup class="bstar">*</sup> <strong>B*</strong>: kernel solve sourced from the generic OpenRouter kernel (no hand-written native driver for this provider) &mdash; distinct from true <strong>B</strong> (kernel-cpu, native driver).</p>

    <div class="totals" id="totals"></div>

    <section class="results-summary">
      <h2>Results</h2>

      <h3>Key findings (v7.6.0)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Anthropic, apples-to-apples</strong> (over both-solved cells): opus &minus;17% cost / &minus;49% tokens at solve parity; sonnet &minus;38% / &minus;65% with kernel solve 93%&rarr;100%.</li>
        <li><strong>Capability multiplier for weak tool-users</strong>: devstral 19%&rarr;97% through the kernel &mdash; 25 tasks the native CLI failed, the kernel solved.</li>
        <li><strong>Solve held or improved</strong> everywhere comparable: gemini 97%&rarr;100%, gpt-5.5 94%&rarr;97%; kimi 97%&rarr;95% is the lone slight regression.</li>
        <li><strong>Token win is universal; cost win is cache-dependent</strong> &mdash; native's volume is mostly cheap cache-read, so the cost gap trails the token gap.</li>
        <li><strong>This is a floor</strong> &mdash; the cache-sliver projection is not yet exercised in the kernel arm.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Methodology</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>38 Docker benchmarks with real bugs (<code>test.sh</code> exits 0 = fixed). 2 legacy pre-kernel tests retired.</li>
        <li><strong>Native</strong>: vendor CLI with its own key. <strong>Kernel (B)</strong>: ostk with native CpuDriver. <strong>B*</strong>: ostk via generic OpenRouter (no native driver for that provider).</li>
        <li>Cost summed per token bucket (fresh 1&times;, cache-read 0.1&times;, cache-create 1.25&times;/2&times;) on a rate card validated to &lt;0.5% of real Anthropic billing.</li>
        <li>Efficiency &Delta; computed only over cells <em>both</em> arms solved; split-resolve, both-fail, and zero-work infra cells excluded.</li>
        <li>Cost/token &Delta; shown only for Anthropic &mdash; gemini-cli / codex / opencode native arms don't report cost (solve-rate only).</li>
        <li>ostk under-reports its own cost ~13%; figures here use the corrected per-bucket recompute, not ostk's self-estimate.</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top:0.8rem;"><a href="/v760.html">&rarr; Full verified results, per-cell tables, and caveats (v7.6.0)</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  main { max-width: none; padding: 1rem 1.5rem 2rem; }

  .visually-hidden {
    position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px;
    padding: 0; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0,0,0,0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0;
  }

  .experiment-info { font-size: 0.85rem; max-width: 800px; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .experiment-info p { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; }

  .lb-container {
    overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--bg); -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
  }

  #lb { border-collapse: separate; border-spacing: 0; min-width: 100%; font-size: 0.72rem; }

  /* Group headers */
  .group-header {
    text-align: center !important; font-size: 0.6rem; padding: 0.3rem 0.4rem !important;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border) !important; letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }
  .group-native { background: rgba(248,81,73,0.08); color: #f85149; }
  .group-kernel { background: rgba(210,153,34,0.08); color: #d29922; }
  .group-cpu { background: rgba(63,185,80,0.08); color: #3fb950; }

  /* B* marker: generic OpenRouter kernel (no native driver) */
  .bstar { color: #d29922; font-weight: 700; cursor: help; }
  .bstar-note { font-size: 0.7rem; margin: 0.4rem 0 0; }

  #lb th {
    padding: 0.4rem 0.4rem; font-size: 0.6rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase; background: var(--surface); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
    white-space: nowrap; cursor: pointer; user-select: none; text-align: right;
  }
  #lb th.sorted { color: #d4a054; }
  #lb th:first-child { text-align: left; }
  #lb th[title] { cursor: help; }
  #lb th.last { border-right: 2px solid rgba(139,148,158,0.2); }

  /* Sticky model column */
  .col-model, #lb td:first-child {
    position: sticky; left: 0; z-index: 2; background: var(--surface);
    min-width: 150px; width: 150px;
  }
  #lb th:first-child { z-index: 3; }

  .col-price { min-width: 45px; }
  .col-solve { min-width: 52px; text-align: center !important; }
  .col-metric { min-width: 50px; }
  .col-delta { min-width: 45px; text-align: center !important; }

  /* Arm column tinting */
  .arm-native { background: rgba(248,81,73,0.03) !important; }
  .arm-kernel { background: rgba(210,153,34,0.03) !important; }
  .arm-cpu { background: rgba(63,185,80,0.03) !important; }
  td.arm-native { background: rgba(248,81,73,0.03) !important; }
  td.arm-kernel { background: rgba(210,153,34,0.03) !important; }
  td.arm-cpu { background: rgba(63,185,80,0.03) !important; }
  td.last { border-right: 2px solid rgba(139,148,158,0.15); }

  #lb td {
    padding: 0.3rem 0.4rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.68rem; white-space: nowrap; text-align: right;
  }
  #lb tr:nth-child(even) td { background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.015); }
  #lb tr:hover td { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); }
  #lb tr:hover td:first-child { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 94%, white); }

  .model-name { font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--text); }

  .solve-pct { font-weight: 700; }
  .pct-100 { color: #3fb950; }
  .pct-90  { color: #3fb950; }
  .pct-70  { color: #d29922; }
  .pct-50  { color: #db6d28; }
  .pct-30  { color: #f85149; }
  .pct-0   { color: #484f58; }
  .pct-na  { color: #30363d; font-weight: 400; }

  .delta-pos { color: #3fb950; font-weight: 600; }
  .delta-neg { color: #f85149; font-weight: 600; }
  .delta-zero { color: #484f58; }

  .dim { color: #484f58; }

  .totals { font-size: 0.78rem; margin: 0.5rem 0; color: var(--text-muted); font-family: var(--mono); }

  .arm-comparison {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 1rem 0; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  .arm-card {
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
  }
  .arm-card h4 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 0.7rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .arm-card .big { font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .arm-card .detail { font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.5; }

  .results-summary { max-width: 800px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .results-summary h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .results-summary h3 { margin: 1rem 0 0.4rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .results-summary ul { padding-left: 1.5rem; margin: 0.4rem 0; }
  .results-summary li { margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .arm-comparison { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    main { padding: 0.5rem; }
    .col-model { width: 100px; min-width: 100px; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  interface ArmAgg { solved: number; total: number; cost: number; tokens: number; tools: number; turns: number; wall: number; }
  interface ModelData {
    model: string; model_normalized: string; benchmarks: number;
    native: ArmAgg; kernel: ArmAgg; cpu: ArmAgg;
    price_per_m_input?: number; price_per_m_output?: number;
    native_cli?: string; cpu_driver_status?: string;
    // B vs B* labeling (frontier-2026): "native_driver" → true B (kernel-cpu),
    // "generic_kernel" → B* (kernel via OpenRouter, no native driver).
    kernel_arm_type?: string;
  }

  function fmtN(n: number): string { return n >= 1e6 ? (n/1e6).toFixed(1)+'M' : n >= 1e3 ? (n/1e3).toFixed(0)+'k' : String(n); }
  function fmtT(s: number): string { return s >= 3600 ? (s/3600).toFixed(1)+'h' : s >= 60 ? (s/60).toFixed(0)+'m' : Math.round(s)+'s'; }
  function fmtUsd(n: number): string { return n >= 10 ? '$'+n.toFixed(0) : n >= 1 ? '$'+n.toFixed(2) : n > 0 ? '$'+n.toFixed(3) : ''; }
  function pctClass(pct: number): string { return pct >= 100 ? 'pct-100' : pct >= 90 ? 'pct-90' : pct >= 70 ? 'pct-70' : pct >= 50 ? 'pct-50' : pct > 0 ? 'pct-30' : 'pct-0'; }

  function armPct(a: ArmAgg): number { return a.total > 0 ? a.solved / a.total * 100 : -1; }

  function solveCell(a: ArmAgg, cls: string, label?: string, bStar?: boolean): string {
    if (a.total === 0) {
      if (label === 'no_driver') return `<td class="${cls} col-solve"><span class="pct-na" title="No native CPU driver for this provider">no driver</span></td>`;
      return `<td class="${cls} col-solve"><span class="pct-na">-</span></td>`;
    }
    const pct = armPct(a);
    // B* marker: generic OpenRouter kernel (no native driver) — distinguish
    // from true B (kernel-cpu). See footnote below the table.
    const star = bStar ? `<sup class="bstar" title="B*: generic OpenRouter kernel, no native driver">*</sup>` : '';
    return `<td class="${cls} col-solve"><span class="solve-pct ${pctClass(pct)}">${a.solved}/${a.total}</span>${star}</td>`;
  }

  function metricCells(a: ArmAgg, cls: string): string {
    if (a.total === 0) return `<td class="${cls}"><span class="dim">-</span></td><td class="${cls}"><span class="dim">-</span></td><td class="${cls} last"><span class="dim">-</span></td>`;
    const cost = fmtUsd(a.cost);
    const tok = a.tokens > 0 ? fmtN(a.tokens) : '-';
    const turns = a.turns > 0 ? String(a.turns) : '-';
    return `<td class="${cls}">${cost || '<span class="dim">-</span>'}</td><td class="${cls}">${tok}</td><td class="${cls} last">${turns}</td>`;
  }

  async function init() {
    const resp = await fetch('/board-v760.json');
    const data = await resp.json();
    const rows: any[] = data.models;

    function deltaSpan(d: number): string {
      if (d == null) return '<span class="dim">—</span>';
      if (d < 0) return `<span style="color:#3fb950;font-weight:700">${d}%</span>`;
      if (d > 0) return `<span style="color:#f85149;font-weight:700">+${d}%</span>`;
      return '<span class="dim">0%</span>';
    }
    function solvePct(solved: number, scored: number, p: number, star: string): string {
      return `<span class="solve-pct ${pctClass(p)}">${solved}/${scored}</span>${star} <span class="dim">${p}%</span>`;
    }

    let sortKey = 'kernel_pct';
    let sortDir = -1;
    const sortVal = (r: any) => {
      if (sortKey === 'model' || sortKey === 'type' || sortKey === 'native_cli') return r[sortKey];
      if (sortKey === 'cost_delta' || sortKey === 'tok_delta') return r[sortKey] ?? 999;
      return r[sortKey] ?? -1;
    };
    const sort = () => rows.sort((a: any, b: any) => {
      const av = sortVal(a), bv = sortVal(b);
      if (av === bv) return 0;
      return sortDir * (typeof av === 'string' ? av.localeCompare(bv) : av - bv);
    });

    const render = () => {
      sort();
      document.getElementById('lb-body')!.innerHTML = rows.map((r: any) => {
        const star = r.type === 'B*' ? '<sup class="bstar" title="generic OpenRouter kernel, no native driver">*</sup>' : '';
        const nat = r.native_dead
          ? '<span class="pct-na" title="native key-blocked — no provider API key">key-blocked</span>'
          : solvePct(r.native_solved, r.scored, r.native_pct, '');
        const ker = solvePct(r.kernel_solved, r.scored, r.kernel_pct, star);
        const costD = (r.cost_trusted && r.cost_delta != null) ? deltaSpan(r.cost_delta)
          : `<span class="dim" title="native cost not reported by ${r.native_cli}">—</span>`;
        const tokD = (r.cost_trusted && r.tok_delta != null) ? deltaSpan(r.tok_delta) : '<span class="dim">—</span>';
        const notes: string[] = [];
        if (r.native_dead) notes.push('native key-blocked — kernel-only');
        else if (!r.cost_trusted) notes.push('solve-rate only');
        if (r.split_kernel_only) notes.push(`kernel solved +${r.split_kernel_only} native missed`);
        if (r.split_native_only) notes.push(`native solved +${r.split_native_only} kernel missed`);
        return `<tr>
          <td><span class="model-name">${r.model}</span></td>
          <td>${r.type}</td>
          <td><span class="dim">${r.native_cli}</span></td>
          <td class="arm-native col-solve">${nat}</td>
          <td class="arm-cpu col-solve">${ker}</td>
          <td class="arm-cpu col-metric">${costD}</td>
          <td class="arm-cpu col-metric">${tokD}</td>
          <td style="text-align:left;font-size:0.64rem;color:var(--text-muted);white-space:normal">${notes.join('; ')}</td>
        </tr>`;
      }).join('');
      document.querySelectorAll('#lb-head th').forEach(th => {
        th.classList.toggle('sorted', (th as HTMLElement).dataset.key === sortKey);
      });
    };

    document.querySelectorAll('#lb-head th').forEach(th => {
      th.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const key = (th as HTMLElement).dataset.key;
        if (!key || key === 'notes') return;
        if (sortKey === key) sortDir *= -1;
        else { sortKey = key; sortDir = (key === 'model' || key === 'type' || key === 'native_cli') ? 1 : -1; }
        render();
      });
    });

    render();

    const tEl = document.getElementById('totals');
    if (tEl) tEl.textContent = `${rows.length} models · ${data.published_tasks} benchmarks · single-shot · v7.6.0 (2026-06-15)`;
  }

  init();
</script>
